<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady on poor arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady on poor arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Wednesday were steady in thin trade and poor arrivals due to rain, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were up by 100 rupees per tonne on increased demand in local markets. The supply was easy from solvent plants and refineries while the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices dropped by $5 per tonne on poor export demand and was down by 100 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. Soymeal yellow was $285 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction prices also fell by $2-3 per tonne in export and quoted at $105-106 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,650 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
